# ouroboros#187 residual, lifted in round 119: a `for` binder over a
# function local, interrogated, body only reads. The VM loop-scopes the
# binder: 7 8, then the local's own 1, then prev 7. Round 116 REFUSED this
# (the post-loop read is the other binding's value only if that binding
# ran first, and the emitter could not tell); the round-117 per-call
# boundness bit is exactly that fact, so it is emitted now. The two shapes
# where the other binding did NOT run first die on both sides: t226, t227.
define f(q) as:
    local r is q
    for r in [7, 8]:
        print of r
    print of r
    print of (prev of r)
    return 0
f of 1
